nt"></span>Overview</p><h2 class="text-3xl leading-tight sm:text-4xl">Why dog health ai matters</h2></div><div class="space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground"><p>A Great Dane and a Jack Russell share almost nothing physiologically. Dog Health AI applies breed-group models so that a resting heart rate of 70bpm is read correctly as unremarkable in one animal and worth investigating in another.</p><p>Gait analysis is the differentiator for dogs. Subtle asymmetry in stride cadence is the earliest reliable indicator of joint disease, and it is measurable long before a visible limp develops.</p></div></div></div></section><section class="py-20 sm:py-24 bg-card"><div class="container-page"><div class="max-w-2xl"><p class="mb-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent"><span aria-hidden="true" class="h-px w-6 bg-accent"></span>Capabilities</p><h2 class="text-3xl leading-tight sm:text-4xl">What this includes</h2></div><ul class="mt-12 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-3"><li><div class="rounded-3xl border border-border bg-card p-7 shadow-soft transition-all duration-300 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lift h-full"><h3 class="text-lg">Gait symmetry analysis</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Stride cadence and weight-shift patterns compared against your dog's own walking signature.</p></div></li><li><div class="rounded-3xl border border-border bg-card p-7 shadow-soft transition-all duration-300 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lift h-full"><h3 class="text-lg">Cardiac trend tracking</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Resting and sleeping heart rate trends, the most sensitive early cardiac marker in dogs.</p></div></li><li><div class="rounded-3xl border border-border bg-card p-7 shadow-soft transition-all duration-300 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lift h-full"><h3 class="text-lg">Breed-group baselines</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Separate models for toy, working, brachycephalic and giant breeds.</p></div></li><li><div class="rounded-3xl border border-border bg-card p-7 shadow-soft transition-all duration-300 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lift h-full"><h3 class="text-lg">Heat and exertion safety</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Exertion warnings weighted for brachycephalic risk and local temperature.</p></div></li><li><div class="rounded-3xl border border-border bg-card p-7 shadow-soft transition-all duration-300 hover:-translate-y-1 hover:shadow-lift h-full"><h3 class="text-lg">Appetite and hydration</h3><p class="mt-3 leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Bowl-level intake tracking that separates a fussy day from a downward trend.</p></div></li></ul></div></section><section class="py-20 sm:py-24 bg-primary text-primary-foreground"><div class="container-page"><div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-2 lg:items-center"><div><p class="mb-4 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent">Outcomes</p><h2 class="text-3xl leading-tight sm:text-4xl">What owners typically see</h2><ul class="mt-8 space-y-4"><li class="flex gap-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-primary-foreground/85"><span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-3 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"></span>Orthopaedic change detected before visible lameness in the majority of monitored cases.</li><li class="flex gap-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-primary-foreground/85"><span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-3 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"></span>Objective evidence for weight-management and mobility plans.</li><li class="flex gap-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-primary-foreground/85"><span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-3 h-1.5 w-1.5 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-accent"></span>Fewer emergency visits caused by heat stress in high-risk breeds.</li></ul></div><img alt="PawlogicTech hardware used for dog health ai" class="w-full rounded-3xl object-cover shadow-lift" decoding="async" height="900" loading="lazy" src="<?php echo esc_url( get_template_directory_uri() ); ?>/assets/images/tech-sensor.webp" width="1200"/></div></div></section><section class="py-20 sm:py-24"><div class="container-page"><div class="grid gap-12 lg:grid-cols-[0.8fr_1.2fr]"><div class="max-w-2xl"><p class="mb-4 inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent"><span aria-hidden="true" class="h-px w-6 bg-accent"></span>FAQ</p><h2 class="text-3xl leading-tight sm:text-4xl">Dog Health AI questions</h2></div><div class="divide-y divide-border rounded-3xl border border-border bg-card"><details class="group px-6 py-5"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-6 text-left font-display text-lg">Which dog sizes are supported?<span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-1 shrink-0 text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45"><svg class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"></path></svg></span></summary><p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">Dogs from 2.5kg upwards. Collar modules ship in three sizes, and the underlying models adjust for toy through giant breed groups.</p></details><details class="group px-6 py-5"><summary class="flex cursor-pointer list-none items-start justify-between gap-6 text-left font-display text-lg">Does gait analysis need a treadmill or clinic visit?<span aria-hidden="true" class="mt-1 shrink-0 text-accent transition-transform duration-200 group-open:rotate-45"><svg class="h-5 w-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.8" viewbox="0 0 24 24"><path d="M12 5v14M5 12h14"></path></svg></span></summary><p class="mt-3 max-w-3xl leading-relaxed text-muted-foreground">No. It is derived passively from everyday walks, which is exactly why it catches change that a single clinic assessment misses.</p></details></div></div></div></section><section class="py-20 sm:py-24 bg-card"><div clas